# Repository Maintenance Plan: Strata Engine

## 1. GGUF Reader Architecture Guard Enhancement

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp` - `check_architecture` function

**Responsibilities:** Validates that a GGUF file matches the expected `qwen4exp` architecture by checking metadata keys against compiled-in constants. Currently performs presence-only checks for expert counts (when want=0) and validates six key fields.

**Proposed Change:** Add validation of `qwen4exp.attention.compression_ratios` consistency with `qsa_interval`, and verify `general.alignment` is a power-of-two within reasonable bounds. Add a `Qwen4ExpGuard` field for expected compression ratio.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_reader.hpp
@@ struct Qwen4ExpGuard {
     uint32_t block_count = 48, hidden = 2560, experts = 0, experts_used = 0, head_count = 24,
-             head_count_kv = 2;   // 0 = presence-only: pruned variants (GSQ-RCO Coder) legitimately ship
+             head_count_kv = 2, compression_ratio = 0;   // 0 = presence-only: pruned variants (GSQ-RCO Coder) legitimately ship
                                   // fewer experts than the canonical 512; the graph reads the true value
 };

 inline std::string check_architecture(const GgufFile& g, const Qwen4ExpGuard& want = {}) {
     const MetaValue* arch = g.get("general.architecture");
     if (!arch) return "missing general.architecture";
     if (arch->s != "qwen4exp") return "architecture is '" + arch->s + "', this engine requires 'qwen4exp'";
     struct Req {
         const char* key;
         uint64_t want;
     };
     const Req reqs[] = {
         {"qwen4exp.block_count", want.block_count},
         {"qwen4exp.embedding_length", want.hidden},
         {"qwen4exp.expert_count", want.experts},
         {"qwen4exp.expert_used_count", want.experts_used},
         {"qwen4exp.attention.head_count", want.head_count},
         {"qwen4exp.attention.head_count_kv", want.head_count_kv},
     };
     for (const auto& r : reqs) {
         const MetaValue* v = g.get(r.key);
         if (!v) return std::string("missing ") + r.key;
         if (r.want && v->u != r.want)
             return std::string(r.key) + " = " + std::to_string(v->u) + ", expected " + std::to_string(r.want);
     }
+    // Validate alignment is a power of two within [1, 256]
+    if (const MetaValue* a = g.get("general.alignment")) {
+        if (a->u == 0 || (a->u & (a->u - 1)) != 0 || a->u > 256)
+            return "general.alignment = " + std::to_string(a->u) + " is not a power of two in [1,256]";
+    }
+    // Verify compression ratios array if present and guard specifies expected ratio
+    if (want.compression_ratio) {
+        const MetaValue* cr = g.get("qwen4exp.attention.compression_ratios");
+        if (!cr) return "missing qwen4exp.attention.compression_ratios";
+        if (cr->type == MetaType::ARRAY && cr->count > 0) {
+            for (uint64_t i = 0; i < cr->count && i < cr->items.size(); ++i) {
+                if (cr->items[i].u != want.compression_ratio)
+                    return "qwen4exp.attention.compression_ratios[" + std::to_string(i) + "] = " +
+                           std::to_string(cr->items[i].u) + ", expected " + std::to_string(want.compression_ratio);
+            }
+        }
+    }
     return {}; // empty == ok
 }
```

**Verification Cases:**
1. Construct a synthetic GGUF with `general.alignment = 48` (not a power of two) and confirm `check_architecture` returns the error string `"general.alignment = 48 is not a power of two in [1,256]"`.
2. Build a GGUF with valid `qwen4exp.attention.compression_ratios` array containing all 4s, set `want.compression_ratio = 4`, and confirm the function returns empty string (pass); then build one with a ratio of 2 at index 5 and confirm the error names that index.

