## 2. GGUF Split Path Validation for Non-Zero Shard Numbers

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` - `gguf_split_paths` function

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the set of shard paths for a split GGUF model given any shard's path. Validates shard numbering format and checks existence of all shards.

**Proposed Change:** Add validation that the total shard count `n` does not exceed a reasonable maximum (e.g., 256), and that when `n == 1` the file doesn't have a split suffix pattern suggesting corruption. Also verify shard file sizes are nonzero.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
     static const char tag[] = "-of-";
     const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
     // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension
     if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
         any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
         return {any};
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
         if (a < '0' || a > '9' || b < '0' || b > '9') return {any};
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
-    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    if (n > 256)
+        throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: split model declares " + std::to_string(n) + " shards, exceeding the "
+                                 "maximum of 256");
+    if (n == 1 && no == 1) {
+        // A single-shard file with split naming is valid but suspicious; verify it opens
+        std::ifstream test(any, std::ios::binary);
+        if (!test)
+            throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: split-named single shard " + any + " cannot be opened");
+    }
     std::vector<std::string> out;
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
         std::snprintf(num, sizeof num, "%05d", i);
         std::string p = any;
         p.replace(at - 5, 5, num);
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
+        // Reject zero-byte shards: a partial download left an empty file
+        std::ifstream chk(p, std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);
+        if (chk.tellg() == 0)
+            throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: model shard " + p + " is empty (size 0); delete it and re-download");
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
 }
```

**Verification Cases:**
1. Create a path string with `00999-of-00999` (999 > 256) and confirm `gguf_split_paths` throws with "exceeding the maximum of 256".
2. Create a valid split model where shard 2 of 3 is a zero-byte file, and confirm the error message contains "is empty (size 0)".

